  "body": "Found by the high-tier review of PR #1183 (review comment on that PR, head f65044b0); not in that PR's lines, and older than it.\n\n**What is wrong.** In `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` the live-tool branch of the section end (about lines 461-469 at that head) returns before `afterOp()`. `afterOp()` is what writes the optional stop (M01), the program stop (M00) and the go-home move a user asked for after an operation. So after a live-tool operation (cross drill, C-axis milling) none of them is posted, and the pending request is carried over: it comes out after the NEXT section, in a place the user did not ask for.\n\n**Why P0.** Wrong posted output with a person at the machine: an operator who asked for a stop after the cross drill (to clear chips, check a hole, flip a part) gets a program that runs straight on into the next operation, and a stop somewhere else.\n\nDone means: a stop or go-home requested after a live-tool section is posted at the end of that section, in the same order the turning branch uses, and nothing carries over into the next section; pinned by a test with a turning section, a live-tool section with M01, M00 and go-home requested in turn, and a following section, plus a recorded case in the per-post script suite; check `tormach-lathe.cps` and the mill posts for an early return of the same kind.",
